  },
  data: {
    LLM: '1. Setup: Six players in two teams of three; each team chooses a captain (rais). Deal three cards to each player; turn one card for trump (briscola).\n2. Play: Trick-taking as in Briscola (follow suit if possible; otherwise play any card). Winner of each trick leads next. At end of each trick, each player draws one card from the stock (winner draws first).\n3. Rais: The rais of each team may ask partners questions and give orders (as in four- and six-player Briscola); only the rais may speak except when answering the rais. When stock is exhausted, the rais may look at the cards of one partner (usually to his right).\n4. Scoring: Same card values as Briscola (Ace 11, Three 10, King 4, Queen 3, Jack 2); team with more points in tricks wins the deal.',
    Player: '1. Setup: Six players in two teams of three; each team chooses a captain (rais). Deal three cards to each player; turn one card for trump (briscola).\n2. Play: Trick-taking as in Briscola (follow suit if possible; otherwise play any card). Winner of each trick leads next. At end of each trick, each player draws one card from the stock (winner draws first).\n3. Rais: The rais of each team may ask partners questions and give orders (as in four- and six-player Briscola); only the rais may speak except when answering the rais. When stock is exhausted, the rais may look at the cards of one partner (usually to his right).\n4. Scoring: Same card values as Briscola (Ace 11, Three 10, King 4, Queen 3, Jack 2); team with more points in tricks wins the deal.',
    objective: 'As in Briscola: win tricks to score points; the team with the higher total when the stock is exhausted and all tricks are played wins the deal.',
    gameplay: '1. Setup: Six players in two teams of three; each team chooses a captain (rais). Deal three cards to each player; turn one card for trump (briscola).\n2. Play: Trick-taking as in Briscola (follow suit if possible; otherwise play any card). Winner of each trick leads next. At end of each trick, each player draws one card from the stock (winner draws first).\n3. Rais: The rais of each team may ask partners questions and give orders (as in four- and six-player Briscola); only the rais may speak except when answering the rais. When stock is exhausted, the rais may look at the cards of one partner (usually to his right).\n4. Scoring: Same card values as Briscola (Ace 11, Three 10, King 4, Queen 3, Jack 2); team with more points in tricks wins the deal.',
